# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore
#
# Controls what enters the build context. This matters for three separate
# reasons, which is why the file is more than an optimisation:
#
#   1. Correctness  - a host `node_modules/` built for Windows or macOS will
#                     break the Linux image if it is copied in.
#   2. Security     - a real `.env` in the context could be baked into a layer
#                     and would then be readable by anyone with the image.
#   3. Build time   - a smaller context transfers faster and produces a more
#                     reproducible build because fewer host files can influence it.
#
# The entrypoint pattern is the reverse of .gitignore: everything is excluded,
# and the files the image genuinely needs are re-included at the end.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control and tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
.editorconfig

# Dependencies are (re)installed inside the image, never copied in
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every environment file is excluded, including the templates.
#
# The .example files hold only placeholders, but excluding the whole pattern is
# the safer default: it means a developer who renames a template to a real file
# cannot accidentally ship it in an image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Runtime state: the database is environment state, created by migrations
data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# Outputs and caches
coverage
.nyc_output
dist
build
.cache
.tmp
logs
*.log

# Local documentation and operations artefacts that the runtime does not need
preview-*
docs/screenshots
*.pdf

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include what the image needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!package.json
!src
!public
!scripts
!docker
!VERSION
